          "detail": "The video explains the Baader-Meinhof phenomenon where your brain, after learning a new word or seeing a specific car, starts 'filtering' it into your conscious awareness, making it look like a global coincidence.\nHook (en): It’s not a coincidence.\nHook (fr): Ce n'est pas une coïncidence.\nWhy: Relatable 'glitch in the matrix' experiences drive high engagement and comments. Users often experience this and think it's fate; explaining the science behind it satisfies curiosity instantly."
