          "id": "halo-effect",
          "label": "2. Why Beauty Blinds Your Judgment",
          "detail": "It reveals the Halo Effect: a cognitive bias where we automatically attribute positive traits like intelligence or kindness to attractive people without any evidence.\nHook (en): Good looks are deceiving you.\nHook (fr): La beauté te trompe.\nWhy: Social dynamics and 'pretty privilege' are currently trending topics on TikTok and Reels. It challenges the viewer's own fairness, making it highly shareable."
        },
        {
          "id": "ikea-effect",
          "label": "3. Why You Overvalue Your Own Work",
          "detail": "The video shows that we value products we helped create—even if they are flawed—much more than identical items built by experts, known as the IKEA Effect.\nHook (en): You overvalue things you build.\nHook (fr): Tu surestimes ce que tu crées.\nWhy: Explaining why we keep 'junk' or feel proud of minor DIY tasks is a universal 'lightbulb' moment. It appeals to both the DIY community and business-minded viewers."
        }
